---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../../consts';
---

<Base title="Mellow privacy policy" description="Privacy policy for Mellow, the dark mode and two-page view extension for Google Docs.">
  <h1>Mellow privacy policy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 22 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      Mellow is a Chrome extension that changes how Google Docs™ looks on your screen: a dark theme
      and an optional two-page view.
    </p>

    <h2>What Mellow collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. Mellow does not collect, store, sell or share any personal data, document content,
      browsing history or usage analytics. It has no servers and makes no network requests of its own.
    </p>

    <h2>What Mellow stores</h2>
    <p>
      Two settings, dark mode on or off and two-page view on or off, saved in your own Chrome profile
      using Chrome's built-in storage so they apply across your documents. Uninstalling Mellow removes them.
    </p>

    <h2>Where Mellow runs</h2>
    <p>
      Only on Google Docs document pages (docs.google.com/document). It changes colours and page
      layout on your screen; it does not read, change or send the contents of your documents.
    </p>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Mellow is free. The optional supporter link opens a checkout run by Polar, which handles that
      payment under its own privacy policy. Mellow itself never sees payment details.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></p>

    <p class="muted">Google Docs is a trademark of Google LLC. Mellow is not affiliated with Google.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
